#
# Failing control for math:TensorAxisIndexRangeConstraint: a rank-2 shape declares two
# axes at indices 0 and 2. Two axes agree with the rank, both indices are zero or
# greater and they differ, so the count, bound and uniqueness laws hold; index 2 is
# not below rank 2 and is the only defect. Bound by ex:ecTensorAxisIndexOutOfRank.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/tensor-shape-controls/> .

ex:shape a math:TensorShape ; math:tensorRank 2 ;
    math:shapeAxis ex:first, ex:third .
ex:first a math:TensorAxis ; math:axisIndex 0 .
ex:third a math:TensorAxis ; math:axisIndex 2 .
